WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.277
REPLACE is useful for direct literal substitution.

00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:11.327
If the source system consistently uses a known abbreviation and the business rule says to expand it,

00:00:11.327 --> 00:00:14.792
REPLACE can be clear and reproducible.

00:00:14.792 --> 00:00:18.082
But it does not understand context.

00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:23.482
For flexible patterns, use regular expressions or a lookup table rather than stacking many fragile

00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:32.367
replacements. String functions are most useful when the text has a predictable structure.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:38.352
Before extracting a substring, confirm the delimiter or pattern really exists.

00:00:38.352 --> 00:00:43.282
Regular expressions are powerful, but a complicated regex can become hard to maintain;

00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:49.232
use the simplest rule that reliably matches the data you actually have.
